<https://ontoboard.org/patterns/pmdco-duality-object-material.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                    dcterms:description "Represents how an object and a portion of matter are the same material entity seen two ways: as material (steel) it bears chemical composition; as object (ingot) it bears mass. Distinguishes extensive qualities, which scale with the size of the object, from intensive qualities, which are independent of portion size."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
                                                                    dcterms:title "Duality of object and material"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label moved to skos:prefLabel x4; label added x8; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title \"Duality of object and material\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
- header: dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> - https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

